{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":106024,"name":"Sergei Zobov","username":"szobov","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discourse.openrobotics.org/szobov/{size}/30947_2.png","created_at":"2025-10-22T23:26:04.277Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey there,\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI’m releasing \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/szobov/ros-opentelemetry\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eros-opentelemetry\u003c/a\u003e, a production-grade library that instruments \u003cstrong\u003eROS 2\u003c/strong\u003e applications with \u003ca href=\"https://opentelemetry.io/docs/what-is-opentelemetry/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eOpenTelemetry\u003c/a\u003e for distributed \u003cstrong\u003etracing,\u003c/strong\u003e correlated \u003cstrong\u003elogs,\u003c/strong\u003e and \u003cstrong\u003emetrics\u003c/strong\u003e — for both \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/szobov/ros-opentelemetry/tree/main/src/ros_opentelemetry_cpp\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eC++\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/szobov/ros-opentelemetry/tree/main/src/ros_opentelemetry_py/ros_opentelemetry_py\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003ePython\u003c/a\u003e nodes.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/original/3X/e/1/e18245875e50e337d7c40b6348225ebea7f1a95f.png\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/waWxg9qS9X9OjpS2wT0gWDuC7VB.png?dl=1\" title=\"image\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/optimized/3X/e/1/e18245875e50e337d7c40b6348225ebea7f1a95f_2_690x391.png\" alt=\"image\" data-base62-sha1=\"waWxg9qS9X9OjpS2wT0gWDuC7VB\" width=\"690\" height=\"391\" srcset=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/optimized/3X/e/1/e18245875e50e337d7c40b6348225ebea7f1a95f_2_690x391.png, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/optimized/3X/e/1/e18245875e50e337d7c40b6348225ebea7f1a95f_2_1035x586.png 1.5x, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/optimized/3X/e/1/e18245875e50e337d7c40b6348225ebea7f1a95f_2_1380x782.png 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"E5E5E2\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003eimage\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e1895×1074 317 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhy this matters\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFollow a task \u003cem\u003eacross nodes\u003c/em\u003e (services, actions, topics) with connected spans.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCorrelate logs with trace/span IDs for rapid root-cause analysis.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBackend-agnostic: send data to any OTel-compatible stack (e.g., SigNoz; Grafana planned).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhat’s inside\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ccode\u003eros_opentelemetry_cpp\u003c/code\u003e and \u003ccode\u003eros_opentelemetry_py\u003c/code\u003e helpers to bootstrap tracers.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ccode\u003eros_opentelemetry_interfaces\u003c/code\u003e with a \u003ccode\u003eTraceMetadata\u003c/code\u003e message to propagate the trace context between nodes.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/szobov/ros-opentelemetry/tree/main?tab=readme-ov-file#instrumenting-code\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eDetailed instructions\u003c/a\u003e on how to instrument your ROS2 code.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e“\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/szobov/ros-opentelemetry/blob/main/Justfile\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eJustfile\u003c/a\u003e” commands + \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/szobov/ros-opentelemetry/tree/main/docker\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eDocker\u003c/a\u003e setup for a one-command demo environment.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDemo\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\nThe repo includes \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/casey/just\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eJust\u003c/a\u003e targets to bring up an \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/szobov/ros-opentelemetry/tree/main/src/example\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eexample\u003c/a\u003e with MoveIt2-based C++ node + a Python task producer instrumented with OpenTelemetry and an OTel stack (e.g., SigNoz).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ccode\u003ejust docker-up-telemetry\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ccode\u003ejust docker-up-example\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eor run locally with \u003ccode\u003ejust run-example-locally\u003c/code\u003e (rViz).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eRepo:\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ca href=\"http://github.com/szobov/ros-opentelemetry\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eROS2 x OpenTelemetry: End‑to‑End Telemetry for Robotics\u003c/a\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cstrong\u003eOpenTelemetry background:\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ca href=\"http://opentelemetry.io\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eopentelemetry.io\u003c/a\u003e (traces/logs, language SDKs)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eHow this relates to existing work\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eComplements \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/ros2/ros2_tracing\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eros2_tracing\u003c/a\u003e (LTTng-based tracing of ROS 2 internals) by offering \u003cstrong\u003evendor-neutral OpenTelemetry\u003c/strong\u003e export and cross-service propagation for app-level spans. If you already use \u003ccode\u003eros2_tracing\u003c/code\u003e, you can keep it for low-level insights and layer OTel for end-to-end visibility.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI’m looking forward to your feedback.\u003cbr\u003e\nAdditionally, I will be presenting this library at \u003ca href=\"https://roscon.ros.org/de/2025/#program\"\u003eROSCon DE\u0026amp;FR 2025\u003c/a\u003e, and I would be happy to discuss it in person.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThanks,\u003cbr\u003e\nSergei\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":2,"updated_at":"2025-10-22T23:26:04.277Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":669,"reads":65,"readers_count":64,"score":3493.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":50658,"topic_slug":"ros2-x-opentelemetry-end-to-end-telemetry-for-robotics","display_username":"Sergei Zobov","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://github.com/szobov/ros-opentelemetry","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"GitHub - szobov/ros-opentelemetry: ROS2 x OpenTelemetry: End‑to‑End Telemetry for Robotics","clicks":80},{"url":"http://github.com/szobov/ros-opentelemetry","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"GitHub - szobov/ros-opentelemetry: ROS2 x OpenTelemetry: End‑to‑End Telemetry for Robotics","clicks":24},{"url":"https://opentelemetry.io/docs/what-is-opentelemetry/","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"What is OpenTelemetry? | OpenTelemetry","clicks":10},{"url":"https://github.com/szobov/ro